<title>USA: UPS, TEAMSTERS TALKS NOT FORMAL SESSION--MEDIATOR.</title>
<headline>UPS, TEAMSTERS TALKS NOT FORMAL SESSION--MEDIATOR.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service managers and striking Teamsters will hold talks on Thursday on the logistics of negotiations rather than holding a formal bargaining session, the chief mediator said.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the kind of meeting where we ask people to check their guns at the door, sit down and make peace. It is not a formal bargaining session,&quot; mediator John Calhoun Wells told reporters outside the Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service.</p>
<p>The two sides are set to meet at the conciliation service at 2 p.m. EDT (1800 GMT) on Thursday. Teamsters workers have been on strike since Monday, after contract negotiations broke down late on Sunday.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8310))</p>
